1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,740
We're finally back!

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,840
The air up here is so much better than the dungeons.

3
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,440
Is this sunrise or sunset?

4
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,800
Do not touch the window. The spell is still in effect here.

5
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:18,640
Kabro, I'm reporting to the Island Lord tomorrow.

6
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:21,320
I'd like you to join me as a witness.

7
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,540
Do you plan on telling him about everything?

8
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,300
I don't think it's necessary to mention Laios and his party.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,900
Mostly, I just don't want Fallon to murder anyone else.

10
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,560
That makes sense.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,060
Why don't you use the rest of the day to get some sleep?

12
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,680
Oh! See that, Kuro?

13
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,520
Big ship. It's huge.

14
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,040
I wonder if the people on it have lots of money!

15
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:48,020
This isn't good.

16
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:52,320
Toshiro, we need to see the Island Lord right away.

17
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:54,440
Is that ship special?

18
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:56,780
It belongs to the Elves of the West.

19
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,100
That bird figurehead.

20
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:01,640
Must be the Canaries, then.

21
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:05,940
They appear when dungeons reach a certain level of danger.

22
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,160
When that happens, their mission is to investigate the dungeon and conquer it.

23
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:14,740
I've heard rumors that they've been putting pressure on the Island Lord.

24
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:17,300
But it looks like they're switching to coercion.

25
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,760
How is something like that allowed?

26
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:21,880
Isn't this a Tall Man region?

27
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:25,940
To the Elves and Dwarves, races with short lives are like infants.

28
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:29,580
And sadly, the Island Lord is not very good at negotiating.

29
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,260
Let's hurry.

30
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:35,000
Huh?

31
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:35,020
Huh?

32
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,160
Hey!

33
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,520
If it isn't Shuro!

34
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:39,940
Hello, Nomari.

35
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:41,780
Where's Fallon?

36
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:47,640
Laios and the others haven't given up yet, though.

37
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,020
That's so.

38
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:52,940
They still eating monsters?

39
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,340
Yes, they are.

40
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:57,400
Excuse me, but we're here to see the Island Lord.

41
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:59,480
Oh, you're out of luck, then.

42
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:02,820
Some important people suddenly came to talk with him.

43
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,160
And they've been in there for hours now.

44
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,300
So we're too late.

45
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:09,000
We have to go inside.

46
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,400
Is that really wise?

47
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:13,100
If the Elves take control of the dungeon, it's over.

48
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:17,520
The town I'm from also prospered from a dungeon.

49
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:21,860
One day, monsters flooded the town.

50
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,080
The Elves came and many died.

51
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:27,540
Why was my family part of the ones who were killed?

52
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:32,240
My mother was a single parent and did everything she could to raise me.

53
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,860
She didn't deserve to die like that.

54
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:38,580
I vowed to never let that happen again.

55
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:42,440
The system in which a single race holds all the power,

56
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,340
it isn't healthy for anyone.

57
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:54,720
Forgive me, but I've come here to deliver a report to the Island Lord.

58
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:58,400
Excuse me?

59
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:00,980
As you can see, we're in the middle of something.

60
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,340
Come back later.

61
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:05,220
It's a report about the situation in the dungeon.

62
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,040
Please, hear me out.

63
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:08,560
Seriously?

64
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,680
Stand your ground.

65
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,000
Make it brief.

66
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:16,920
Not too long ago, during our exploration,

67
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,780
we encountered a human who turned into a monster.

68
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:21,160
What?

69
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:22,980
Damn it.

70
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:23,800
A chimera.

71
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,900
It's progressing faster than expected.

72
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:26,520
See?

73
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:27,780
I told you all!

74
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,600
We didn't have time to twiddle our thumbs and wait for an answer!

75
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,380
Let's give the order to make landfall.

76
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:33,620
We won't allow that!

77
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,560
The elderly need not get worked up.

78
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,720
Country borders are so trivial compared to the lives of people.

79
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:43,240
Just who do you think you are, treating me like I'm old and senile?

80
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,540
Tonsu, please.

81
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:45,960
I think we've said enough.

82
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:46,540
What the?

83
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:50,260
You're a true island lord, understanding and wise.

84
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,480
Now, if you would please stamp here.

85
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,180
Don't do it!

86
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,520
You can't give in!

87
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:57,640
Did we actually end up making things worse here?

88
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,480
The truth is...

89
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,100
If I had enough strength to conquer a dungeon,

90
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,820
there wouldn't be a problem.

91
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:05,620
But I don't.

92
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:10,680
So I started looking around for adventurers who were more skilled that I could assist.

93
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:16,020
However, most of the people I found were self-serving and worthless.

94
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,260
By the time I accepted my fate and tried to conquer the dungeon myself,

95
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,300
I heard rumors about the Toten siblings.

96
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:26,140
I have a feeling that they were brought up pretty well.

97
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,900
They have good instincts, but no real ambition.

98
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,660
They're honestly kind of weird.

99
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:34,420
The more I found out, the stranger they seemed.

100
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:38,780
Despite not being that strong, they reached the deeper floors of the dungeon.

101
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:41,840
They would give money to people with poor reputations,

102
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:45,500
and their origins in the strange company they kept were hard to follow.

103
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:49,460
Still, there's something about the brother that made me feel

104
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:52,040
he was deeply connected to the destiny of this island.

105
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:55,780
The question was, would his role be good or bad?

106
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:59,320
To decide that, I wanted to speak with him directly.

107
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,820
And once I did, I finally understood.

108
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,060
He only thinks about monsters.

109
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:09,400
Therefore, we can't trust him to consider the future of the island.

110
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,580
But there's one thing I can say for sure.

111
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:17,040
At this moment, among the Tall Men, he's the one who's closest to the heart of the dungeon.

112
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:20,760
This will more than likely be the first and last chance we get,

113
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,960
so I can't let the elves get in his way.

114
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:26,260
I'll figure out what to do about him after.

115
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:28,380
Enough already.

116
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,600
You can do whatever you want.

117
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,500
My lord!

118
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,000
I'll let them know to make landfall.

119
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:33,880
Please, wait!

120
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:34,600
Huh?

121
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,220
It's too dangerous.

122
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:39,640
The types of monsters, architecture, and environments.

123
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,040
All of it's in turmoil.

124
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:42,880
We're already aware of this.

125
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,420
It's a characteristic of dungeons showing growth.

126
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,700
We have to stop it as soon as possible.

127
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:50,020
In human terms, a growth spurt.

128
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:52,740
This is when it requires the most nutrients.

129
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:54,080
What's all this now?

130
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:56,080
About 15 years ago,

131
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,920
a dungeon destroyed my hometown.

132
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:01,540
It was a town called Utaya.

133
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,340
15 years ago?

134
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:04,480
Then what did that mean?

135
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,280
No way!

136
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,420
Are you the child they see survived that incident?

137
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:11,340
I did hear that the vice captain or someone had brought a young one home with them.

138
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:12,120
Yes.

139
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,060
They took care of me for several years.

140
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:15,040
Oh?

141
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,060
You were probably spoiled, but became an adventurer.

142
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:21,400
It was my dream to join a squad, but I couldn't as a tall man.

143
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:24,000
I didn't want to repeat that tragedy,

144
00:06:24,420 --> 00:06:25,880
so I wanted a way to help.

145
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,440
How admirable.

146
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,040
Are you getting enough to eat?

147
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,700
You should go and visit the vice captain sometime!

148
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,520
Anyway,

149
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:36,660
you mentioned nutrients.

150
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,140
Tell me more.

151
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:41,040
Well, because of your efforts,

152
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,240
Utaya's dungeon was quickly destroyed.

153
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:43,820
However,

154
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:47,040
there were many casualties among the soldiers and civilians.

155
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:51,600
It was due to the dead turning into monsters and eating the living.

156
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:55,640
Soldiers were ambushed before they could do anything.

157
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:59,400
Rely on numbers and Utaya will repeat itself.

158
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,720
I suggest we seal the dungeon instead.

159
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:05,060
We can't do anything that will end up feeding it.

160
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:09,720
I'm pretty sure it's not your intention to cause damage to the dungeon during combat anyway.

161
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,120
How many people are inside?

162
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,400
The majority of them are on the first floor.

163
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:16,620
Let's evacuate them slowly.

164
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:19,300
All humans have some sort of connection.

165
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:22,800
And I know some people who can definitely help out.

166
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,860
So just leave it to me!

167
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:29,480
Cabro,

168
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:33,360
he still ate monsters despite everything he went through?

169
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,400
Begin preparations

170
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:39,820
for the investigation.

171
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:40,340
Huh?

172
00:07:40,340 --> 00:07:43,920
I suspect you're plotting something.

173
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,660
If that's the case,

174
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:46,960
show me what you've got.

175
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,100
Should anything go wrong,

176
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,840
my troops will rush in.

177
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,180
Understood.

178
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:53,580
Yes.

179
00:07:53,580 --> 00:08:04,340
So are they like scrambled eggs?

180
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,100
Huh?

181
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:08,620
You said before that people compare souls to eggs.

182
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,600
But if you're referring to souls that are mixed together,

183
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:14,280
then what would that mean in relation to how eggs are cooked?

184
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:15,680
For example,

185
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:16,700
scrambled eggs,

186
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:18,060
a sunny-side-up egg,

187
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:18,900
and a poached egg

188
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,500
would all have different stories.

189
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,700
Listen, Senshi.

190
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,240
I didn't make that comparison

191
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,520
for you to take what I said

192
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,020
and try to make a joke out of it.

193
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:27,340
Who's making jokes?

194
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,000
I was actually impressed

195
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,880
by how interesting a comparison it was.

196
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,300
There's nothing else that behaves

197
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:35,320
in as many different ways as an egg does.

198
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:36,360
For example,

199
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,000
eggs get firm when heated,

200
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,820
but the white and yolk solidify

201
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:40,880
at different temperatures.

202
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:41,840
Frothiness,

203
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:42,860
moisture retention,

204
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:43,620
viscosity,

205
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:45,800
and the most interesting one,

206
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,280
emulsification.

207
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,640
Even things that don't mix naturally

208
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,820
like oil and water

209
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:51,800
mixed beautifully

210
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:52,920
under the right conditions.

211
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,620
Just like this.

212
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:55,640
Well, that's...

213
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,540
Wait, souls are actually nothing like eggs.

214
00:08:59,100 --> 00:08:59,580
Laios,

215
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:01,120
you mind handing me that bread there?

216
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,380
It's ready.

217
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:19,760
So, how are we supposed to eat this?

218
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:21,940
Pick up the bread with your knife and fork,

219
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:24,600
then use the bread to scoop the yolk and sauce

220
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,100
as you eat.

221
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,760
Delicious as usual.

222
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,460
If you don't mind,

223
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:38,480
could you stop looking around at stuff

224
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,480
that isn't really there?

225
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:40,820
Or is there something?

226
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,380
I don't think so.

227
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:44,860
I just thought I felt some kind of presence.

228
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:45,500
Huh?

229
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:49,380
Does that mean this isn't a hallucination?

230
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,160
Huh?

231
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:55,320
Well, when I'd gotten mana sickness,

232
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:56,780
remember when I mentioned

233
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,300
I was seeing and hearing things?

234
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:00,340
That never went away.

235
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,080
Seriously?

236
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:02,420
Why didn't you say something?

237
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:04,360
Because Chill would just yell at me

238
00:10:04,360 --> 00:10:05,560
and tell me I'm sick in the head.

239
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:06,820
That's because you are.

240
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,380
What are you hallucinating?

241
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:13,800
Day in and day out,

242
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:15,500
something keeps trying to talk to me.

243
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:18,080
At first, I couldn't tell what it was saying.

244
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,800
But gradually,

245
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:21,960
its voice and shape started getting clearer.

246
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:23,380
It's pretty scary,

247
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:25,360
so I've been pretending not to see it.

248
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,840
Then you could actually hear me speaking after all.

249
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:31,340
So what did it say?

250
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:34,540
Well, it's not too happy that I was ignoring it.

251
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:36,720
I wonder if talking to it is okay.

252
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,960
Do you think it's evil?

253
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,620
Uh, not sure.

254
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:40,740
Possibly.

255
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,140
Hello there!

256
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:44,700
Can I help you with something?

257
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:46,000
Uh-huh.

258
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:48,660
What's it saying now?

259
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:52,240
It's mad at me because I thought it was an evil ghost.

260
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:53,540
Also,

261
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,200
it's asking if we've forgotten

262
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:58,340
that it saved us from the, uh, mage.

263
00:10:58,760 --> 00:10:59,160
Huh?

264
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,240
Oh, wait!

265
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,080
I remember!

266
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:03,200
Right.

267
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:04,800
How could I forget that whole thing?

268
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,320
Please give it our thanks.

269
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,040
Hmm.

270
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:07,780
Mm-hmm.

271
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,240
I guess it wants to introduce us to someone?

272
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:11,420
Thoughts?

273
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,560
It's not the god of death, is it?

274
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:14,140
Well,

275
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:16,220
we don't have many options, so...

276
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:16,680
All right.

277
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,000
We're ready to go whenever you are.

278
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:48,980
We're ready to go whenever you are.

279
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:50,380
Oh!

280
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:56,620
What?

281
00:11:57,620 --> 00:11:58,300
Wait.

282
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,600
What the heck?

283
00:12:00,060 --> 00:12:01,180
Where are we?

284
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:01,900
Hey!

285
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,920
Out of the road, please!

286
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,340
Is that a unicorn?

287
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:10,660
That clothing.

288
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:12,440
Did you guys come from the outside?

289
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:13,280
No.

290
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,440
We came from the dungeon and...

291
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,640
I can't believe it.

292
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:17,800
Come with me.

293
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:28,020
I've never seen monsters be this docile before.

294
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,120
It's because they're ordered not to hurt us,

295
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,540
so we can coexist here.

296
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,280
Whoa.

297
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,760
That's not going to be the case for outsiders, though.

298
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:37,400
So make sure you hold on to the stuff I gave you.

299
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,440
Izutsumi?

300
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:40,600
Something wrong?

301
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,320
Teleportation sickness?

302
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:43,900
She's probably tired.

303
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:47,320
Is that the Golden Castle?

304
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:48,300
Sure is.

305
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:51,100
And the ghosts that brought us to this place,

306
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,280
are they actual residents, too?

307
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:54,300
Pretty much.

308
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:55,100
Well,

309
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:57,560
the person you're about to meet has more info.

310
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,820
Maybe they'll know why you were chosen,

311
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:01,120
because we sure don't.

312
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:02,800
We were chosen?

313
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,420
This is it.

314
00:13:05,720 --> 00:13:06,640
Just sit tight, okay?

315
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:11,140
If you're looking for the master,

316
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:12,340
he went to the church.

317
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:15,580
It's them.

318
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:16,320
Huh?

319
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:17,740
Those guys?

320
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,340
Guess we came here at a pretty bad time.

321
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:23,680
Until the master comes back here,

322
00:13:23,860 --> 00:13:25,620
why don't you try to relax in the village?

323
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,420
Seems like everyone really wants to show you

324
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,120
their hospitality.

325
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:32,160
What should we take them around to see first?

326
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:34,560
The village isn't that special, so...

327
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,420
They're all residents of the Golden Castle?

328
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,520
Yeah, but I don't see any old folk.

329
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:40,460
Honestly, I'd like to see

330
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,980
where the monsters are being raised.

331
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:42,460
Huh?

332
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,740
I want to take a tour of the fields

333
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:45,920
we saw on the way over.

334
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:46,880
Huh?

335
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,520
That's what you're interested in?

336
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:50,560
I mean, that's easy enough.

337
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:51,500
Hooray!

338
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,320
I'll just wait for them to get back.

339
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:57,640
Can't leave he's a tsumi alone anyway.

340
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,760
I agree.

341
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,180
That's a minotaur!

342
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:02,640
And it's female!

343
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:05,900
We milk this instead of cows.

344
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,440
Why are you raising monsters?

345
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,740
Oh, because normal livestock

346
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:11,100
was hard to get a hold of.

347
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:11,620
Oh!

348
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,260
Oh!

349
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:22,160
What a beautiful field.

350
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:23,960
It's so well tended to.

351
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:26,860
Is everything here used up by the villagers?

352
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:29,480
We admittedly waste quite a lot of it.

353
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:31,940
But if we didn't have fields to keep us busy,

354
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:32,960
we'd have nothing to do.

355
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,720
It's mostly an appearance,

356
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:36,760
but we try to mimic surface life.

357
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:37,420
Really?

358
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:41,940
Isutsumi, are you okay?

359
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:47,200
At least she doesn't seem sick, I guess.

360
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,280
Sorry!

361
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,420
We don't mean to interrupt, but...

362
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,580
Dresses?

363
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:55,360
Exactly!

364
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:57,360
They're dresses we made by hand.

365
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,540
We've gotten so bored of modeling them ourselves.

366
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:01,940
We need the fresh face of an outsider to do it.

367
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:03,640
Sure, if you want me to.

368
00:15:05,060 --> 00:15:06,300
Which should we try?

369
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,920
It has to be the red one!

370
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,200
You'll have to forgive us.

371
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:11,620
Our dresses might seem a little old-fashioned

372
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:12,500
from your perspective.

373
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,180
I'm sure it's fine.

374
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,060
Somehow this is different than what I expected.

375
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,180
Guess this is what happens

376
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:25,380
when you've been isolated for a thousand years.

377
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:26,980
Try this on next!

378
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,660
This is great!

379
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:34,000
I'm pretty picky about my alcohol,

380
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,580
but this isn't bad at all.

381
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:36,640
Happy to hear.

382
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:38,700
I've been serving it to my Orc customers,

383
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,780
and this recent batch is really popular among them.

384
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:44,320
Yeah, I bet.

385
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:45,760
Oh, what about wine?

386
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:46,680
Do you make that?

387
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,720
Well, I do,

388
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,500
but it's much newer than making ale.

389
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:51,660
Been doing that 400 years now,

390
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,440
so making the switch has been tricky.

391
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,820
That long, huh?

392
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,440
Sounds pretty established.

393
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,040
What generation are you?

394
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,840
I started it when I was 600,

395
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,120
so first generation.

396
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:02,900
Come again?

397
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,660
Chilchuk, guess what?

398
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,100
They let me milk a minotaur!

399
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:08,560
Hey, good for you.

400
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:10,180
Keep that to yourself next time.

401
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,660
This place is incredible!

402
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:14,740
They've completely succeeded in cultivating monsters

403
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:15,700
and made it an art!

404
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:16,840
Do you see that?

405
00:16:16,840 --> 00:16:19,480
It's the biggest dryad garden I've ever seen!

406
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,820
The minotaur had four nipples like a cow!

407
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,460
I'm not feeling so good.

408
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:27,740
That was a once-in-a-lifetime experience.

409
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,080
You really missed out?

410
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:30,240
By the way,

411
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,620
where did the other two go?

412
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,800
What's with the weird non-sequitur?

413
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,020
Uh, we're over here.

414
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:42,480
What in the hell are you wearing?

415
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:43,700
Playing dress-up, huh?

416
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:44,500
Don't misunderstand!

417
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,500
I was asked to wear this, I swear!

418
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:50,500
I actually, this was the tamest one I tried on.

419
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,380
Marcelle, you, uh...

420
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:55,180
Uh, yeah?

421
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,060
Lyos?

422
00:16:58,020 --> 00:17:00,540
You have any clue why she's stuck to you like that?

423
00:17:00,780 --> 00:17:01,920
Oh, that, right!

424
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:03,420
Yeah, I have no idea!

425
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,240
That's so weird!

426
00:17:04,240 --> 00:17:08,240
Uh, it's like she switched brains with a child or something!

427
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:09,060
Uh!

428
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:09,920
Oh!

429
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:11,120
Yeah!

430
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:15,360
Lots of barriers have been cast here in many different layers.

431
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:18,940
And it seems like it's affecting Izutsumi in some way.

432
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,360
It's because she's half-monster, right?

433
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:22,000
Yeah.

434
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:26,560
But I've never seen a barrier make monsters non-aggressive before.

435
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:30,080
I really wish I could decipher this.

436
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:32,580
But I don't know most of these characters,

437
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:34,020
and I don't have time to learn!

438
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:37,660
Why the hell do these things have to be so hard to read and secretive?

439
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,160
Anyway, this really is an amazing place.

440
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,360
Under different circumstances,

441
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,700
I wouldn't mind staying here forever.

442
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:48,360
Same here.

443
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:56,260
My apologies for the long wait.

444
00:17:56,660 --> 00:17:57,420
It isn't much,

445
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,460
but we've prepared a warm meal for all of you.

446
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,680
This way, please.

447
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:06,780
Ah, welcome, everyone.

448
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:08,480
I've been wanting to meet you.

449
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,560
I'm Yod.

450
00:18:09,660 --> 00:18:10,300
It's a pleasure.

451
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,640
You already know of Delgol, yes?

452
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,220
Well, he's my grandfather.

453
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:15,600
Delgol?

454
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,500
Please, feel free to take a seat.

455
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:20,100
You're wondering why I've called you here.

456
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,420
This will take some time to explain.

457
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:24,300
Let's see it first.

458
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:32,840
Uh, is this meat?

459
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:33,520
Yes!

460
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:35,680
As your party had specifically requested,

461
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:37,600
we prepared Minotaur meat!

462
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:42,880
Does everyone in the village routinely eat monsters, too?

463
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:44,560
There are some who do,

464
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:47,180
although we don't really need to consume food.

465
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:47,720
Huh?

466
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,660
Our sense of taste has completely dulled.

467
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:52,000
Aside from that,

468
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:54,160
we have no real appetite to speak of.

469
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,920
Such is the curse of immortality

470
00:18:56,920 --> 00:19:00,020
that the mad mage cast on the people of this village.

471
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:05,120
Do you know why the mage would do something like that?

472
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:05,720
No.

473
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,440
When I grew old enough to know what was happening,

474
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,320
the mage was already in a state

475
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:12,380
where communicating with him was difficult.

476
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:16,420
But please, don't let our problems stop you.

477
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,060
Go eat up to your heart's content.

478
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,800
We may not get hungry,

479
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:22,140
but simply being able to watch others eat

480
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:23,280
still brings us joy.

481
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:25,640
Well, now, I definitely can't say

482
00:19:25,640 --> 00:19:27,360
that I don't really want to eat this.

483
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,360
Grandfather.

484
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,980
For as long as I can remember,

485
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,940
he always blamed himself

486
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:37,940
for being the one who made the mad mage

487
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:39,760
become obsessed with black magic.

488
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:41,700
So in order to look for help,

489
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,080
he headed to the surface.

490
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:46,340
Perhaps you know.

491
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:47,760
How did he fare up there?

492
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,660
Well, from what I've heard,

493
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:52,500
he was seen emerging from the underground cemetery.

494
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:55,200
He claimed he was the king of a ruined country

495
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,880
and would give his entire kingdom

496
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:59,020
to the one who defeated the mad mage,

497
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:00,420
then turn to dust.

498
00:20:01,180 --> 00:20:02,100
Is that so?

499
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:05,200
He's finally been released from his agony.

500
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:07,440
Knowing this brings me solace.

501
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,380
Many people have attempted to escape the curse

502
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:11,600
by leaving the village.

503
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,700
However, none have succeeded

504
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:16,340
and their physical bodies are lost as a result.

505
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:20,240
Without a body, you gradually lose yourself,

506
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,880
become an evil ghost,

507
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:24,400
and then are unable to return here.

508
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:27,400
I'm sure you've encountered these ghosts before.

509
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:28,200
Yeah.

510
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:30,560
We attacked them with holy water

511
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:32,240
and then made us for a bay out of them.

512
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,560
So, anyway,

513
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:37,540
you never told us why we were called to this place.

514
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:38,540
The prophecy.

515
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:39,640
Prophecy?

516
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:40,580
Indeed.

517
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,740
One shall arrive at the village

518
00:20:42,740 --> 00:20:44,360
with winged sword in hand.

519
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,880
They will be the hero

520
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,580
who will defeat the mad mage

521
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,800
and set us all free.

522
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:50,040
Winged sword.

523
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,340
Does he mean Kensuke?

524
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:53,540
Well, there are wings on it, although...

525
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:54,920
Wait!

526
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:56,960
This lion face wasn't on here before!

527
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:58,540
When did...

528
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:02,060
The winged lion is our guardian deity.

529
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:05,180
He was imprisoned at the very bottom of the dungeon

530
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,400
by the mad mage.

531
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:07,260
However,

532
00:21:07,580 --> 00:21:09,280
the lion still guides us

533
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:10,540
by telling us prophecies

534
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,760
by way of our dreams.

535
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:14,100
And those prophecies are why

536
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:16,120
my grandfather left for the surface.

537
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:18,680
Sir Laios,

538
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:20,680
there is more to the prophecy.

539
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,580
With the winged sword in their hand,

540
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,200
the hero will defeat the mad mage

541
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:29,400
and thus rise as the country's new king.

542
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:30,920
Wait!

543
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:32,120
You can't be serious!

544
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,580
He just picked up that sword by complete accident!

545
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:35,800
It was no accident.

546
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,780
The fact the sword is in this room with us

547
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,540
means it was something preordained.

548
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,180
Now, Sir Laios,

549
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:46,720
can you please promise me something?

550
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:49,800
Promise me you'll defeat the mad mage

551
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:52,060
and free everyone in this village!

552
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:54,920
But I...

553
00:21:54,920 --> 00:22:03,220
Can you please let me think about it?

554
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:05,680
You gotta turn him down.

555
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,880
Why bother giving them hope like that?

556
00:22:08,220 --> 00:22:10,220
Because I can't flat-out refuse.

557
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:11,420
Kensuke,

558
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:13,580
when'd you even get like this?

559
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:14,160
Huh, buddy?

560
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,520
Maybe it was when you got eaten

561
00:22:16,520 --> 00:22:17,820
by the dungeon cleaners.

562
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:22,380
I was actually so nervous during all that,

563
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:24,460
I couldn't really taste any of the food

564
00:22:24,460 --> 00:22:25,360
they made for us.

565
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:27,700
You've got some nerve, you know that?

566
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:30,060
Specifically requested by the party, huh?

567
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:32,720
It really didn't have that much flavor

568
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:33,540
to begin with.

569
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:34,360
Huh?

570
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:35,880
You said they have no appetite,

571
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,340
so they don't need to eat anything.

572
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:39,540
I think it's safe to assume

573
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:41,240
that's why they're not very good at cooking.

574
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:43,920
I just realized something.

575
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:46,080
The people in this village,

576
00:22:46,260 --> 00:22:48,140
they don't really need to tend fields

577
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:49,100
and use dishware,

578
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:50,960
so why bother keeping them around?

579
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:53,600
What was the point in wasting all that energy

580
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:55,160
to continue maintaining them

581
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:56,960
for the last thousand years or so?

582
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:00,740
I reckon it's because they actually do need those things.

583
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:03,000
It helps them keep their sanity

584
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,320
and gives them a reason to live.

585
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:07,600
Laios,

586
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:10,960
when we were with the Orc Chief on the third floor,

587
00:23:11,460 --> 00:23:13,900
I still remember exactly what you told them.

588
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:17,660
What did I say again?

589
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:18,360
Well,

590
00:23:18,580 --> 00:23:21,080
make sure you take the night to think about it.

591
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:25,460
Do you mind if I sleep in here, too?

592
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,300
Go sleep in the room they gave you.

593
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,340
But I don't want to be alone in there.

594
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,140
And Izutsumi's being weird.

595
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,500
Come on, scoot over.

596
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:33,680
Just sleep on the floor.

597
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,480
His hands were so cold.

598
00:23:36,480 --> 00:24:06,460
I don't want to be alone in there.

